# Copy to /etc/lalabase-backup/backup.conf on BOTH hosts and adjust.
# Values only — this file is sourced by the backup scripts. No secrets here: the
# private age key never touches a server, and the SSH key is referenced by path.
#
# Why this file exists: the Storage Box sub-account is an operator's coordinate,
# not part of the product. Hardcoding it in the scripts meant a published copy of
# this repo would carry our account. The `: "${VAR:=…}"` form assigns only when the
# variable is not already set, so an environment override keeps winning — which is
# what ops/backup/test/run-tests.sh relies on.

# Storage Box sub-account for THIS host. Each host gets its own, jailed to its own
# directory: the DB host writes db/, the app server writes attachments/. A taken
# over app server must not reach the database dumps, and the other way round.
: "${REMOTE:=uXXXXXX-subN@uXXXXXX.your-storagebox.de}"

# Private half of the SSH key registered with that sub-account. Mode 600, root-owned.
: "${SSH_KEY:=/root/.ssh/id_ed25519_storagebox}"

# DB host only: the database lalabase-db-backup.sh dumps.
: "${DB_NAME:=lalabase_production}"

# App server only: the Active Storage directory lalabase-attachments-backup.sh
# mirrors, inside the deploy root (<deploy root>/shared/storage).
: "${SRC:=/home/deploy/lalabase_production/shared/storage}"
